===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To make a clumsy or stupid mistake.
#: ''to '''blunder''' in preparing a medical prescription''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To move [[blindly]] or [[clumsily]].
#* Goldsmith
#*: I was never distinguished for address, and have often even '''blundered''' in making my bow.
#* Dryden
#*: '''blunders''' on, and staggers every pace
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To cause to make a mistake.
#* Ditton
#*: To '''blunder''' an adversary.
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To do or treat in a blundering manner; to confuse.
#* Stillingfleet
#*: He '''blunders''' and confounds all these together.

